    "result": "I implemented `check_password` in `solution.py` following the spec. It raises `TypeError` for non-`str` password or username, then checks LENGTH (12–64 inclusive), CLASSES (at least 3 of lowercase, uppercase, digit, other, with non-ASCII counting as other), USERNAME (username of 3+ characters found in the password, both lowercased), REPEAT (three or more identical characters in a row, case-sensitive) and BLOCKLIST (exact equality after lowercasing, not containment). Violations are returned in spec order. I wrote `tests/test_solution.py` with 19 pytest cases covering each rule, its boundaries, the case-sensitivity and containment edge cases, and rule ordering. Running `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 19. I only edited `solution.py` and files under `tests/`, and installed nothing. The first draft of the tests had several miscounted inputs; I rewrote them before the run, so the passing run reflects the corrected file.",
